   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Hard Times** (1 review): The reviewer says the second track of the opening set is Hard Times, a John Legend song [4]\n- **Everytime I See You I Go Wild** (1 review): The reviewer says the sixth track of the opening set is a Stevie Wonder song, Everytime I See You I Go Wild [4]\n- **Take A Chance -> $** (1 review): George Porter reportedly confirmed that the song between Funkify Your Life and Africa is Take A Chance, not Come Fly With Me [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **intro by Nigel Hall**: back after 69 archived shows (1047 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Hard Times**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Everwhere I Go**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **banter - thanks to Victor**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **My Love**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Surely**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Everytime I See You I Go Wild**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **thanks**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-03-08.tlm170.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 34 songs; 169 min [1]\n- **soulive2012-03-08.mk21.flac24**: audience recording; 20 songs; 171 min [3]\n- **soulive2012-03-08.mk21.flac16**: audience recording; 20 songs; 171 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Alecia Chakour and the Osrah played the opening set; the horn section was James Casey, Ryan Zoidas and Eric Bloom [1]\n- Guests included Kofi Burbridge, Citizen Cope, Alice Smith, Nigel Hall, George Porter Jr, Billy Martin and ?uestlove on drum kit [1]\n- This was night 8 of Bowlive 3; the Alecia Chakour Band opened, then Soulive played two sets with the Bowlive Horns [2]\n- Guests were Kofi Burbridge on flute and percussion, Citizen Cope, Alice Smith, Nigel Hall, George Porter Jr. and Billy Martin [2]\n- This was night 8 of Bowlive 3; the Alecia Chakour Band opened, then Soulive played two sets with the Bowlive Horns [3]\n- Guests were Kofi Burbridge on flute and percussion, Citizen Cope, Alice Smith, Nigel Hall, George Porter Jr. and Billy Martin [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-03-08.tlm170.flac16**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: FOB Audience [1]. Also: Hand-scrubbed to remove 96 audience claps, spread across tracks in both sets [1]\n- **soulive2012-03-08.mk21.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [3]. Also: This is a 24-bit transfer, not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning; a CD-quality version exists separately [3]\n- **soulive2012-03-08.mk21.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]",
